From 9f38ab033b08ae30ce2fc62d0150520239d6a5c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bradley Gleave <bradley@bradleytgpcoaching.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:55:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(s5-r3): assert claim-race terminal contract,
 deterministic refused down, real detached O fixture

Validation-only follow-up to 485c6797 (S5 R2 audit findings); no src/, prisma/ or workflow change.

- rls-g2-pg17-etq0: the claim-race characterization now awaits the T worker and asserts each
  branch's terminal contract instead of logging it: down-applied => worker failure
  {500, Internal server error, P2022}, no result, no completion event, zero ledger rows, zero
  targets, column absent, history 165, then forward repair; down-refused => column and catalog
  intact, exactly one ledger row whose status is coupled to the target/result/event
  (reconstructed, or failed with error:Prisma.P2028 and no target). Both branches converge on a
  T replay minting exactly one reconstructed row bound to one Person. The 500/P2022 outcome is
  labelled as characterization of a state a rollout must never enter, not acceptable behaviour.
- New deterministic refused-branch test: the fixture worker holds its claim past E's 5 s
  lock_timeout (txTimeout, fixture-only), down is refused with a lock timeout leaving column,
  catalog, history and visibility untouched, and the released claim then commits whole.
- g2-tq0-worker.cjs: optional fixture-only txTimeout passed to Prisma $transaction only when the
  service passes no options.
- New test/utils/g2-pg17-old-root.sh: creates/verifies the preserved-O fixture as a detached
  Git checkout of 925780e0 (self-contained local clone by default) and runs bootstrap's step-4
  identity gate offline; a git archive extraction is rejected because it cannot pass that gate.
- Spec beforeAll reads the confirmed port from the guarded target instead of a literal.
- Fixture-owned comments corrected: E's forward file is not idempotent (rerun fails closed);
  --single-transaction is redundant around a file with its own BEGIN/COMMIT. Recovery text
  remains S1-owned and is untouched.
